{"id":"000VLQ","title":"Mind the Edge ! #7","author":"Todd","solvedCount":4,"difficulty":2,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-10-19T10:52:14+00:00","posted":"Heute, 08:18 Uhr","rules":"Sudoku: Place digits 0–8 so that each digit appears exactly once in every row, column, and 3×3 box.\n\nEdge mines: Each digit equals the total number of mines on that cell’s four edges (top, bottom, left, right). Each edge holds 0, 1, or 2 mines.\n\nKiller cages: Digits in a cage do not repeat and sum to the number in the cage’s top-left corner.\n\nMark edges: Only the outside edges of each killer cage are marked — blue = 0 mines, red = 1 mine, red with a × = 2 mines. Mark the remaining edges by yourself (Pen tool under Settings ⚙).\n\nOnline play: https://sudokupad.app/mdfeiqdddr\n\nTIPS: This is a hybrid of Sudoku and Minesweeper. You need both Sudoku rules and the fact that adjacent digits having the same mine count on their common edge. For example, an 8 forces 2 mines on each of its four edges, so none of its four neighbors can be 0 or 1. Likewise, none of the four neighbors of a 0 can be 7 or 8. The figure below shows one possible arrangement of digits in a box, together with mines on edges:\n\nMind the Edge ! #0: 000VE7.\n\nMind the Edge ! #2: 000UZC.\n\nMind the Edge ! #3: 000V0U.\n\nMind the Edge ! #4: 000V33.\n\nMind the Edge ! #5: 000VES.\n\nMind the Edge ! #6: 000VF7.\n\nMore of my games: hitodd.com.","solutionCode":"The mine counts on all horizontal edges of column 9, read top to bottom (10 numbers, each 0–2).","tags":["Sudoku","Minesweeper"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/mdfeiqdddr","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/mdfeiqdddr","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":4,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-10-19T10:52:14+00:00"}